{"title":"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Tess runs counterclockwise around rectangular block <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/0073ed91e1a9a1cda445af237b7b67815147c979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JKLM$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" />. She lives at corner <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Which graph could represent her straight-line distance from home?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/a/cfa3151064b41051d0fd988b63693968a5f5531e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(5mm); pair J=(-3,2); pair K=(-3,-2); pair L=(3,-2); pair M=(3,2);  draw(J--K--L--M--cycle); label(&quot;$J$&quot;,J,NW); label(&quot;$K$&quot;,K,SW); label(&quot;$L$&quot;,L,SE); label(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,NE); [/asy]\" width=\"195\" height=\"138\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46f6af01fcf3bb5f6cac2316bc4de9bb3906bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/c/e1ce58d3d8b5534cf365cdcf8118b8edc2afaa55.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(80);defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)); //A draw((16,0)--origin--(0,16)); draw(origin--(15,15)); label(&quot;time&quot;, (8,0), S); label(rotate(90)*&quot;distance&quot;, (0,8), W); [/asy]\" width=\"135\" height=\"135\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b7193f66028e13f331d53ff5e6942c4b05587465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/7/657b9a7866d66252b5a03bb0b4c6b257cbf6504a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(80);defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)); //B draw((16,0)--origin--(0,16)); draw((0,6)--(1,6)--(1,12)--(2,12)--(2,11)--(3,11)--(3,1)--(12,1)--(12,0)); label(&quot;time&quot;, (8,0), S); label(rotate(90)*&quot;distance&quot;, (0,8), W); [/asy]\" width=\"135\" height=\"135\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169b8d69bd74a91e72ec43123070d770633a340a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bff98a36d2d506b16dadd585fc7d43750b30b43b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(80);defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)); //C draw((16,0)--origin--(0,16)); draw(origin--(2.7,8)--(3,9)^^(11,9)--(14,0)); draw(Arc((4,9), 1, 0, 180)); draw(Arc((10,9), 1, 0, 180)); draw(Arc((7,9), 2, 180,360)); label(&quot;time&quot;, (8,0), S); label(rotate(90)*&quot;distance&quot;, (0,8), W); [/asy]\" width=\"135\" height=\"135\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b305929a95b53f14a0ad53eba1d8560626e1f28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/f/c4f99af82414203b386ec3abd62914e6b1f85cff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(80);defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)); //D draw((16,0)--origin--(0,16)); draw(origin--(2,6)--(7,14)--(10,12)--(14,0)); label(&quot;time&quot;, (8,0), S); label(rotate(90)*&quot;distance&quot;, (0,8), W); [/asy]\" width=\"135\" height=\"135\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e41e3cd48cee2c6866cfbb4386a8e99d3482f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/d/18dee85d26f1e02bceb105cd20a1bd2880aaee49.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(80);defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)); //E draw((16,0)--origin--(0,16)); draw(origin--(3,6)--(7,6)--(10,12)--(14,12)); label(&quot;time&quot;, (8,0), S); label(rotate(90)*&quot;distance&quot;, (0,8), W); [/asy]\" width=\"135\" height=\"135\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For her distance to be represented as a constant horizontal line, Tess would have to be running in a circular shape with her home as the center. Since she is running around a rectangle, this is not possible, ruling out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with straight lines. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/b/3eb312e2e07da192f08833f89f182303c785afdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JL$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" /> is the diagonal of the rectangle, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is at the middle distance around the perimeter, her maximum distance should be in the middle of her journey. The maximum in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is at the end, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has two maximums, ruling both out. Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693c4044f8526a8179956e8ac7a3f2f9d61e2c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"43\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Even though Solution 1 may find an answer, it is never proven that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> actually describes the distance to Tess' home.\n</p><p>It may be easier to compare the distance traveled by Tess rather than the time spent, if we suppose that Tess moves at constant speed then the graphs distance-time and distance-position are equivalent.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the linear distance walked by Tess, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> her distance from home <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. We will divide this problem into four parts (sections <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/3926a81a9db71d9566f1f34318868691c7f535b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JK$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef091d889893c7c10e475a93e4ef626ff70aa5ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/1/0b1d8f246c1f2c2fbe6fea0847d28a9ab77e8338.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LM$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/1/2f177d5b67a1852a70a5ca32027169a187c16097.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MJ$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />).\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/a/cfa3151064b41051d0fd988b63693968a5f5531e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(5mm); pair J=(-3,2); pair K=(-3,-2); pair L=(3,-2); pair M=(3,2);  draw(J--K--L--M--cycle); label(&quot;$J$&quot;,J,NW); label(&quot;$K$&quot;,K,SW); label(&quot;$L$&quot;,L,SE); label(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,NE); [/asy]\" width=\"195\" height=\"138\" />\n</p><p>Section <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/3926a81a9db71d9566f1f34318868691c7f535b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JK$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />: At any point of the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/3926a81a9db71d9566f1f34318868691c7f535b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JK$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, the distance of Tess from home is described by the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/9/fa9fcf858ec027dad580a9ff31a0a7880dcf41f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{JK}(x)=x_J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/7/29789ff6f87b014f9fc4cff426feac0ed34db717.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> is the linear distance traveled by Tess from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Section <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef091d889893c7c10e475a93e4ef626ff70aa5ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />: From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, the distance from home is described by a right triangle, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the hypotenuse. In this situation the distance follows the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/0/7704c0cdc3304bd41298c8a72ee1a1517f0efe88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{KL}(x)=\\sqrt{JK^2+x_K^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"181\" height=\"35\" />, which is a curve (this was obtained by applying the Pythagorean Theorem).\n</p><p>Section <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/1/0b1d8f246c1f2c2fbe6fea0847d28a9ab77e8338.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LM$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />: Following an analogue reasoning to Section <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef091d889893c7c10e475a93e4ef626ff70aa5ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, the distance function in this case results <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/8/3682ed6560b256728639ee1ab3b0be4a3f2d8e23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{LM}(x)=\\sqrt{MJ^2+(LM-x_L)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"259\" height=\"35\" /> which is also a curve.\n</p><p>Section <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/1/2f177d5b67a1852a70a5ca32027169a187c16097.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MJ$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />: Analogue to Section <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/3926a81a9db71d9566f1f34318868691c7f535b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JK$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, we obtain a linear function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/2/8a2086b79436ba4faffece2a86c265e28bc22902.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{MJ}(x)=MJ-x_M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"162\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>None of the shown answers in the multiple choice describe the real distance between Tess and home along the path.\n</p><p>The real graph should have a shape of the following kind:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/2/e620ffdbf30b062e70b46b5a76f6e5913d8f7a55.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(80);defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)); //D draw((16,0)--origin--(0,16)); draw(origin--(3.2,10.3)^^(10,12.2)--(14,0)); draw(Arc((26.7,1.9), 25, 145, 160)); draw(Arc((12,18), 6, 198, 250)); label(&quot;time&quot;, (8,0), S); label(rotate(90)*&quot;distance&quot;, (0,8), W); [/asy]\" width=\"135\" height=\"135\" />\n</p><p>Which is slightly different from the expected solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~ FaC7oR\nNote:\nWe do not recommend this way\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8\" title=\"2004 AMC 8\">2004 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2004\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017184045\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 301/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2272/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9577/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.213      1 -total\n 57.25%    7.564      1 Template:AMC8_box\n 41.18%    5.441      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11630:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017184045 and revision id 275472. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}